1.2 Data Science Lifecycle + Intro to Generative AI
## 1. Problem statement

**App:** Zomato

**Business problem:** Some users receive orders later than the delivery time shown when ordering. This can reduce customer satisfaction and lead to lower ratings or fewer repeat orders. I would build a data science project to predict delivery delays and identify the factors behind them, so Zomato can show more accurate delivery estimates and address recurring delays.

## 2. Data needed

| Data | Example fields | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Order and delivery records | Order time, promised and actual delivery times, restaurant, delivery distance | Database |
| Restaurant details | Cuisine, preparation time, location, average order volume | Database or API |
| Live traffic and weather | Traffic speed, congestion, rainfall, temperature | API |
| Customer feedback | Ratings and comments after delivery | Database |

## 3. Clean a sample dataset

Since no dataset was provided, here is an illustrative sample of 10 orders:

| order_id | restaurant | delivery_time (min) | rating |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| 101 | Spice Hub | 30 | 5 |
| 102 | Pizza Town | 45 | 4 |
| 103 | Spice Hub | 35 | 4 |
| 104 | Green Bowl | 25 | 5 |
| 105 | Pizza Town | 50 | 3 |
| 106 | Spice Hub |  | 4 |
| 107 | Tasty Dosa | 40 | 4 |
| 108 | Green Bowl | 30 |  |
| 109 | Pizza Town | 55 | 2 |
| 110 | Tasty Dosa | 35 | 5 |

Pandas code to remove rows with any missing value and lowercase restaurant names:

```python
import pandas as pd

df = pd.DataFrame([
    {"order_id": 101, "restaurant": "Spice Hub", "delivery_time": 30, "rating": 5},
    {"order_id": 102, "restaurant": "Pizza Town", "delivery_time": 45, "rating": 4},
    {"order_id": 103, "restaurant": "Spice Hub", "delivery_time": 35, "rating": 4},
    {"order_id": 104, "restaurant": "Green Bowl", "delivery_time": 25, "rating": 5},
    {"order_id": 105, "restaurant": "Pizza Town", "delivery_time": 50, "rating": 3},
    {"order_id": 106, "restaurant": "Spice Hub", "delivery_time": None, "rating": 4},
    {"order_id": 107, "restaurant": "Tasty Dosa", "delivery_time": 40, "rating": 4},
    {"order_id": 108, "restaurant": "Green Bowl", "delivery_time": 30, "rating": None},
    {"order_id": 109, "restaurant": "Pizza Town", "delivery_time": 55, "rating": 2},
    {"order_id": 110, "restaurant": "Tasty Dosa", "delivery_time": 35, "rating": 5},
])

cleaned = df.dropna().copy()
cleaned["restaurant"] = cleaned["restaurant"].str.lower()
```

The two rows with missing values (orders 106 and 108) are removed, leaving **8 orders**.

